86491394 1072 #uuid "71f9aed2-ae1d-5853-b1d1-1e76be4a49fc" 13194139535288 17592186045443 true] [17592186491394 1074 "First, let $u=3x+6.$ Then differentiating with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=3\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{3}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nWe can now rewrite the integral in terms of $u,$ solve it, and write the final answer in terms of $x$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{5}{3x+6}\\,\\text{d}x & =5\\int \\frac{1}{3x+6}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =5\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\cdot (\\frac{1}{3})\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{3}\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u|+C \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|3x+6|+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can further simplify the above by writing $C=\\frac{5}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡K$ for another arbitrary constant $K,$ and then we can combine the two terms using the laws of logarithms, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|3x+6|+C & =\\frac{5}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|3x+6|+\\frac{5}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡K \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{3}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡|3x+6|+\\operatorname{ln}⁡K) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(K|3x+6|)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we finally conclude that\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{5}{3x+6}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{5}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(K|3x+6|).\n$$" 13194139535288 17592186045443 true] [17592186491395 1080 "\\frac{K}{6}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(|6x+2|)" 13194139535288 17592186045443 true] [17592186491395 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535288 17592186045443 true] [17592186491395 1083 #uuid "792e0c84-eee3-5f47-9343-9bd165f08572" 13194139535288 17592186045443 true] [17592186491396 1068 #edb/ref 17592186491402 13194139535288 17592186045443 true] [17592186491396 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139535288 17592186045443 true] [17592186491396 1071 "Calculate $\\int \\frac{1}{3-4x}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Assume that $K$ is an arbitrary positive constant." 13194139535288 17592186045443 true] [17592186491396 1072 #uuid "7b296cf1-22cc-51dc-9bbc-