t $u=6x+2.$ Then differentiating with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=6\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{6}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nWe can now rewrite the integral in terms of $u,$ solve it, and write the final answer in terms of $x$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{6x+2}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\cdot \\frac{1}{6}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u|+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|6x+2|+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can further simplify the above by writing $C=\\frac{1}{6}\\operatorname{ln}⁡K$ for another arbitrary constant $K,$ and then we can combine the two terms using the laws of logarithms, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{6}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|6x+2|+C & =\\frac{1}{6}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|6x+2|+\\frac{1}{6}\\operatorname{ln}⁡K \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡|6x+2|+\\operatorname{ln}⁡K) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(K|6x+2|)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we finally conclude that\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{6x+2}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{6}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(K|6x+2|).\n$$" 13194139535288 17592186045443 true] [17592186491405 1080 "\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(K|3-4x|)" 13194139535288 17592186045443 true] [17592186491405 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535288 17592186045443 true] [17592186491405 1083 #uuid "f10479be-37f6-55c9-9c2d-8dbee457b99a" 13194139535288 17592186045443 true] [17592186491406 1080 "-4\\operatorname{ln}⁡(K|3-4x|)" 13194139535288 17592186045443 true] [17592186491406 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535288 17592186045443 true] [17592186491406 1083 #uuid "fd7dcafd-2ed2-5588-8f0c-3f475682d35d" 13194139535288 17592186045443 true] [17592186491407 1168 "generate/scratch/17592186064207.py" 13194139535288 17592186045443 true] [17592186491407 1169 #uuid "f45d6854-72c3-5483-b143-0dec3a5aeb96" 13194139535288 17592186045443 true]] :edb/tempids {"0e90047e-f55c-52b5-b46c-93db0257557e" 17592186491379 "0ed309